 "datasheet": "Espressif ESP32 Series Datasheet v5.3 (dl/esp32.pdf; https://www.espressif.com/sites/default/files/documentation/esp32_datasheet_en.pdf): Fig 6-2 QFN48 (5x5 mm) p59: D=E 5.00 (4.95-5.05), D2=E2 3.70 (3.65-3.75), b 0.18 (0.13-0.23), L 0.35 (0.30-0.40), e 0.35 BSC, pin-1 C0.35 on the EP; pin layout Fig 2-2 p13 (top view, ESP32-D0WD-V3 is QFN 5*5 per Table 1-1 p3): 14 pins on the left (1-14) and right (25-38) sides, 10 on the bottom (15-24) and top (39-48), pin 49 = GND EP; the data sheet gives NO land pattern",
 "derivation": "IPC-7351B flat no-lead method with the datasheet tolerances (F 0.10, P 0.05): heel G = Smax(rms) - 0.206 = 4.18 -> 4.20 (inner pad edge 2.10, heel goal 0), toe at density L (J_T 0.20 at the body edge): Z = 5.40 = the area budget QFN48_5 5.4 x 5.4 (DESIGN-SPEC 9.2, budget_v6 / sketch_v5), pad width = b nominal 0.18 (DESIGN-SPEC 4.7/8.1: 0.18 mm pads; leaves 0.17 mm copper gap at 0.35 pitch, >= 0.15 SMD pad-pad rule); EP land = D2 nominal 3.70 (0.25 mm to the pin heels); EP paste 3x3 windows 1.00 mm on 1.25 mm pitch = 66 % (stencil 0.10 mm; pins 1:1, area ratio 0.71). Ganged solder-mask opening per pad row (F.Mask rectangle, pads + 0.04) because the mask web at 0.35 pitch would be 0.09 mm < 0.10 (DESIGN-SPEC 8.1/8.4, D43 rule fine_pitch_ganged_mask, active only after the O15 NextPCB EQ); footprint attribute allow_soldermask_bridges set",
